    "featured": false,
    "excerpt": "Understand the chemical and structural differences between Heavy-Duty Commercial Grade and Standard Grade Steel commercial equipment. Learn how choosing the right grade saves lakhs in rust repairs and FSSAI penalties.",
    "quickAnswer": "Heavy-Duty Commercial Grade contains 18% Chromium and 8% Nickel, forming a protective chromium oxide layer that prevents rust and acid corrosion from tomato gravies, citrus, and salt. Standard Grade Steel substitutes Nickel with Manganese and Nitrogen, making it prone to pitting and rust within 18-24 months in humid, salty, and acidic commercial cooking environments.",
